Verified with npm `ggaction@0.0.17`, Node 22.23.1. GitHub `main` resolved to `e539c0b71be569dfc5d82f4180e8a08a8f580c76` on 2026-09-16, the same commit as our pinned official source snapshot. These are authoring improvements found while translating 50 static Vega-Lite charts (47 accepted); they are not new blockers for those accepted charts. We prioritize preserved meaning, visual fidelity, then fewer public actions and explicit options. Synthetic data below is independent of the dataset.

## Problem

Text positions/content can be data-bound, but `encodeColor` rejects text marks. Attached `createMarkLabels` avoids repeating x/y; matching a point's category-dependent stroke still requires one selected label layer per color.

A 14-observation scatter with two decade colors originally needed two filtered datasets and two text/x/y/text chains. Current `createMarkLabels` allows a reduction from ten such actions to two, but each call repeats source, field, selection, fill, alignment, offset and font. One data-bound label layer should be enough for this meaning.

## Executed reproduction

```js
import {chart} from 'ggaction';
chart().createCanvas().createData({values:[
 {x:1,y:2,t:'first',g:'one'}, {x:3,y:4,t:'second',g:'two'}
]}).createTextMark({id:'labels'})
 .encodeChannels({target:'labels',channels:{
   x:{field:'x'},y:{field:'y'},text:{field:'t'}
