## Requested behavior

- Support field-driven text fill/color with existing nominal/ordinal/continuous scale rules, or an equally explicit text appearance encoding.
- For attached labels, allow explicit inheritance of the source's resolved fill or stroke. Preserve existing arc/rect contrast policy; don't globally change readable-label defaults.
- Resolve appearance per source item after filtering/grouping/aggregation and keep it synchronized after source re-encoding, scale edits and rematerialization.
- Define legend ownership so labels do not duplicate a source legend by default.

## Acceptance checks

Two colored point categories produce one attached label layer with corresponding colors, including hollow points whose visible category encoding is stroke. Add constant override, missing-value, selection, resize and source-rebinding checks. Related closed #110/#115 concern existing source-owned position/data behavior; this request concerns appearance capability.

