 .fitCanvas({minPlotWidth:30,minPlotHeight:30});
// The x-axis labels do not fit the Canvas margin.
```

The guide creation fails before `fitCanvas` runs. Existing [fitCanvas](https://github.com/ggaction/ggaction/blob/e539c0b71be569dfc5d82f4180e8a08a8f580c76/src/actions/canvas/fitting.js) searches margins inside a fixed outer canvas; minPlotWidth/Height are lower bounds, not an exact inner-size contract. `applyTextMetrics` already exists and can supply measured text; this proposal should reuse that infrastructure.

## Requested contract

Provide an opt-in layout mode that fixes the authored inner width/height, measures occupied guide/title/legend bounds, then allocates margins and expands the outer canvas. Define constraint priority and overflow behavior when outer dimensions are also fixed. Permit guide authoring to complete before final fit validation, or expose a declarative initial layout equivalent.

Rotated-label anchoring/baseline or automatic offsets should be considered within this contract: current labels expose rotation/offset/wrap/maxWidth but no authorable alignment/baseline. Avoid requiring users to guess several mutually dependent pixel offsets.

## Acceptance checks

- The example retains exactly 30×30 inner dimensions, all labels visible and no collisions.
- Same policy works for -45° labels with axis titles and optional legends/facets.
- SVG and Canvas use consistent measured bounds; resize/font-metric updates are repeatable.
- Existing fixed-outer-size behavior remains compatible.

