## Problem

In `ggaction@0.0.17`, the public point-mark authoring API accepts only the 12 built-in `PointShape` values. It cannot express a data-bound custom SVG pictogram repeated at encoded positions.

This blocks a static Vega-Lite translation of a 10×10 medal pictogram: 100 medals represent Australian Olympic medals, with 97 orange and 3 blue symbols. The original has a 400×400 plot and a compound SVG medal path (ribbon, circular medal, star cutout). Replacing the medal with a built-in circle/star changes the defining pictogram. We have paused only this chart; geographic charts are unrelated and excluded from our project.

This is a request for a public custom symbol API or a documented equivalent recipe, not a claim that the SVG renderer cannot draw paths. We intentionally avoid hand-generating 100 unrelated graphic paths or replaying a source SVG, since the output must retain ggaction data/mark/encoding semantics.

