## Requested behavior

A documented public way to define a normalized custom path symbol and use it through point marks/shape encodings, with ordinary x/y positioning and color/size mappings. The API should define origin, bounds, size normalization and fill-rule behavior so compound pictograms with holes remain reproducible. An explicitly supported registration API would also work; raw arbitrary SVG injection is unnecessary.

Suggested coverage: two repeated custom symbols retain distinct datum identities; custom size/color encodings work; closed subpaths and holes render; invalid paths fail clearly; existing built-in shapes remain unchanged. A public recipe for the 10×10 custom-symbol use case would resolve the translation blocker.

## Problem and impact

A static Vega-Lite stacked area chart with an ordered categorical independent axis cannot be expressed directly with ggaction's area facade or area position encoding in `ggaction@0.0.17`. The representative source uses weekdays `Mon` through `Sun`, quantitative totals, and five sales channels. The category order and readable weekday labels are essential; matching implicit canvas dimensions or pixel-level label placement is not required.

The area facade rejects `fieldType: "ordinal"`; the lower-level `encodeX` rejects it too. A tested numeric-rank alternative draws the area successfully, but adding weekday labels through the public axis `labelMap` fails because that option only accepts categorical scales. We paused this translation after verifying those failures, rather than substituting numeric labels or dropping the categorical axis.

This is a request for native categorical area support (or an officially supported equivalent recipe). It is not a claim that every possible composite/separate-guide workaround is impossible.

