## Problem

Source-owned Text follows final source geometry, but its inherited position encodings are still treated as independent scale consumers. After changing the source field, stale label fields distort the automatic domain. Changing the source to another named scale can also be blocked by its own labels when axes/grid are present, or retain an obsolete scale as a Canvas dependency.

Directly assigning a position to source-owned Text is accepted even though Text materialization continues to use the source anchor. This can leave source and text graphics inconsistent after the resulting scale change.

## Reproduction at 79cdaf81

```js
const base = chart().createCanvas({ width: 480, height: 320, margin: 40 })
  .createData({ values: [
    { x: 1, y: 1, other: 100 },
    { x: 2, y: 3, other: 1000 }
  ] })
  .createPointMark().encodeX({ field: "x" }).encodeY({ field: "y" });
const bare = base.encodeY({ field: "other" });
const labelled = base.createTextMark({ source: "point", text: "label" })
  .encodeY({ target: "point", field: "other" });
```

`bare.resolvedScales.y.domain` is `[100,1000]`, but `labelled.resolvedScales.y.domain` is `[1,1000]`. Adding source-following labels must not change the source's data domain.

A separate reproduction, `base.createTextMark({ source:"point", text:"label" }).encodeY({ target:"text", field:"other" })`, retains `source:"point"` while rewriting the Text encoding. The domain becomes `[1,1000]`; point y positions become `[280,279.5195...]` but Text y positions remain `[280,40]`.

## Required correction

Make source-owned Text an indirect geometry dependent, never an independent scale-domain consumer. Apply the same ownership rule to scale edits, detach/Canvas plans and guide rebinding. Preserve independent text as a real consumer. Reject direct source-owned Text position reassignment before any child changes; authors can edit the source, use Text dx/dy, or create independent Text with explicit data.

Verify current/source-rebound scales, quantitative/category/time data, guides, resize, labels, source removal, and independent text behavior. Keep Bar/Histogram and existing final-item label contracts covered.

